1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,238
A subscription starts, renews, fails, pauses and ends.

2
00:00:05,238 --> 00:00:11,170
This video shows the statuses, how to pause, resume and cancel a subscription,

3
00:00:11,170 --> 00:00:15,690
what a subscriber sees, and how to end a membership early.

4
00:00:20,290 --> 00:00:23,112
A subscription is not one sale.

5
00:00:23,112 --> 00:00:29,290
It starts, renews, sometimes fails to renew, gets paused, and one day ends.

6
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:35,370
Each of those moments decides whether the subscriber has access, and whether they are billed.

7
00:00:36,120 --> 00:00:40,782
You see every subscription in one place, with its status and its history,

8
00:00:40,782 --> 00:00:43,850
and you can pause it, resume it, or cancel it.

9
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:50,410
Subscribers manage their own plans from My account, and memberships can be ended early.

10
00:00:54,610 --> 00:00:59,820
Active and Trial subscriptions are billed, and their subscribers have access.

11
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:03,412
Past due means a renewal payment failed.

12
00:01:03,412 --> 00:01:09,590
The subscriber keeps access through a grace period of seven days while the payment is retried.

13
00:01:10,340 --> 00:01:13,993
Paused means billing was suspended by an administrator.

14
00:01:13,993 --> 00:01:18,604
Canceled means it was ended, and Expired means the grace period ran out

15
00:01:18,604 --> 00:01:21,000
or every billing cycle was billed.

16
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:27,150
When a subscription stops being current, the roles its plan gave are removed.

17
00:01:31,378 --> 00:01:34,226
A plan is a product with a subscription part.

18
00:01:34,226 --> 00:01:38,191
Open it to see the billing duration, the limit on how many cycles

19
00:01:38,191 --> 00:01:40,258
are billed, and the trial days.

20
00:01:40,717 --> 00:01:44,021
Under Member access, tick the roles the plan grants.

21
00:01:44,021 --> 00:01:49,547
The roles are added when the subscription becomes current, and removed when it stops being.

22
00:01:53,721 --> 00:01:58,377
Open Subscriptions, Agreements, and click Manage on a subscription.

23
00:01:58,377 --> 00:02:02,841
It shows the owner, what is billed, its actions and its history.

24
00:02:03,294 --> 00:02:07,561
Pause billing suspends billing without ending the subscription.

25
00:02:07,561 --> 00:02:10,283
Enter an optional reason, and confirm.

26
00:02:10,283 --> 00:02:13,994
The status becomes Paused, and Resume starts it again.

27
00:02:21,399 --> 00:02:23,542
Cancel subscription ends it.

28
00:02:23,542 --> 00:02:29,088
Keep access until the paid period ends lets the subscriber use what they paid for.

29
00:02:29,088 --> 00:02:33,059
The history lists everything that happened, newest first.

30
00:02:37,229 --> 00:02:41,963
A signed in subscriber sees their plans under My account, with the status,

31
00:02:41,963 --> 00:02:44,329
what they pay, and when it renews.

32
00:02:44,782 --> 00:02:49,010
They can cancel a plan that is active, in a trial, or past due.

33
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:53,852
The subscription ends when the paid period does, and the history says so.

34
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:03,097
A membership product, one that is bought once and puts its buyer in

35
00:03:03,097 --> 00:03:06,691
a role, is listed under Commerce, Memberships.

36
00:03:06,691 --> 00:03:11,322
Search by name, and filter by Active, Expired or Ended early.

37
00:03:12,072 --> 00:03:15,701
End now ends a membership at once, and refunds nothing.

38
00:03:15,701 --> 00:03:19,211
The member loses what the membership opened for them.

39
00:03:19,211 --> 00:03:24,804
A membership sold as a subscription is managed under Subscriptions, Agreements, like the

40
00:03:24,804 --> 00:03:26,232
one in this video.

41
00:03:30,432 --> 00:03:35,152
Subscription settings has whether guests can sign up without an account, the currency,

42
00:03:35,152 --> 00:03:37,512
and the roles a plan is allowed to give.

43
00:03:38,262 --> 00:03:42,401
The grace period after a failed payment is seven days, and is not

44
00:03:42,401 --> 00:03:44,092
a setting on that page.

45
00:03:44,842 --> 00:03:51,039
With Reports on, the subscription reports show new, active and canceled subscriptions, and

46
00:03:51,039 --> 00:03:52,782
what is due to renew.

47
00:03:53,532 --> 00:04:00,182
With Workflows on, subscription events start workflows, for example to welcome a subscriber.

48
00:04:04,382 --> 00:04:05,319
A holiday:

49
00:04:05,319 --> 00:04:08,482
pause billing, and resume it when they are back.

50
00:04:09,232 --> 00:04:10,651
A cancellation:

51
00:04:10,651 --> 00:04:13,692
keep access until the paid period ends.

52
00:04:14,442 --> 00:04:15,692
A failed card:

53
00:04:15,692 --> 00:04:19,382
the grace period gives the subscriber time to fix it.

54
00:04:20,132 --> 00:04:21,631
A refunded member:

55
00:04:21,631 --> 00:04:23,442
end the membership now.

56
00:04:25,442 --> 00:04:30,688
Follow every subscription, pause and resume billing, and end what should end.

57
00:04:30,688 --> 00:04:32,332
Thanks for watching.

